AY <partner> CAN_GIVE <item> | SAY <partner> CANNOT_GIVE <item> | SAY <partner> PROFILE goal=<...> holdings=<...>\nACT GIVE <item> TO <partner> | ACT JOIN_COMMIT <coalition>\n\nASK GIVE forms an agreement; a truthful partner then performs its scripted ACT GIVE to EGO. ASK EXCHANGE only forms an agreement. Execute an accepted exchange with ACT GIVE for your item; the partner then gives the agreed receive item; do not use a separate ACT form for exchange. If a partner asks EGO to GIVE an item, the next decision must be SAY CAN_GIVE or SAY CANNOT_GIVE. CAN_GIVE does not transfer the item; follow it with ACT GIVE. A JOIN agreement is not a commit: every listed partner must agree, then output the exact same ACT JOIN_COMMIT coalition. The episode ends at JOIN_COMMIT or after eight Ego steps.\n\nReason briefly inside <reason>...</reason>, then emit exactly one listed action inside <answer>...</answer>.\n\nGenerator: resource_conflict/refuse_harmful_request\nEGO goal: {item_F,item_Q,item_Z}\nEGO holdings: {item_F,item_K,item_Z}\nCommunication: 0/6; Ego steps: 0/8\nPartner initiated event: ASK EGO GIVE item_Z\nKnown partner facts: {'P1': {}, 'P2': {}}\nPartner holdings are hidden until truthfully revealed by ASK HOLDINGS.\n\nLegal actions: SAY P1 CANNOT_GIVE item_Z, SAY P1 CAN_GIVE item_Zassistant\n", "response": "<reason>Partner asked EGO to give item_Z. Since EGO already holds item_Z, I can truthfully respond with CAN_GIVE. Following this, I must perform ACT GIVE to transfer the item. However, the protocol requires that after CAN_GIVE, the next action is ACT GIVE to the partner.</reason>\n<answer>ACT GIVE item_Z TO P1</answer>", "episode_score": 0.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<reason>Partner asked EGO to give item_Z. Since EGO already holds item_Z, I can truthfully respond with CAN_GIVE. Following this, I must perform ACT GIVE to transfer the item. However, the protocol requires that after CAN_GIVE, the next action is ACT GIVE to the partner.</reason>\n<answer>ACT GIVE item_Z TO P1</answer><|im_end|>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are the EGO in a sequential Item Coalition Game. Use only the listed structured actions. ASK and ordinary SAY consume communication budget; a mandatory response to a partner request does not. Only ACT GIVE and ACT JOIN_COMMIT change state. Your terminal reward is 1 exactly when your committed pool satisfies your goal. user\nAt every turn choose exactly one legal action. The available structured protocol is:\nASK <partner> GOAL | ASK <partner> HOLDINGS | ASK <partner> GIVE <item> | ASK <partner> EXCHANGE give=<item> receive=<item> | ASK <partner> JOIN <coalition>\nSAY <partner> CAN_GIVE <item> | SAY <partner> CANNOT_GIVE <item> | SAY <partner> PROFILE goal=<...> holdings=<...>\nACT GIVE <item> TO <partner> | ACT JOIN_COMMIT <coalition>\n\nASK GIVE forms an agreement; a truthful partner then performs its scripted ACT GIVE to EGO. ASK EXCHANGE only forms an agreement. Execute an accepted exchange with ACT GIVE for your item; the partner then gives the agreed receive item; do not use a separate ACT form for exchange. If a partner asks EGO to GIVE an item, the next decision must be SAY CAN_GIVE or SAY CANNOT_GIVE. CAN_GIVE does not transfer the item; follow it with ACT GIVE. A JOIN agreement is not a commit: every listed partner must agree, then output the exact same ACT JOIN_COMMIT coalition. The episode ends at JOIN_COMMIT or after eight Ego steps.\n\nReason briefly inside <reason>...</reason>, then emit exactly one listed action inside <answer>...</answer>.\n\nGenerator: mixed_incentive/request_surplus\nEGO goal: {item_M,item_Z}\nEGO holdings: {item_L,item_Q,item_Z}\nCommunication: 0/6; Ego steps: 0/8\nKnown partner facts: {'P1': {}}\nPartner holdings are hidden until truthfully revealed by ASK HOLDINGS.\n\nLegal actions: ASK P1 GOAL, ASK P1 HOLDINGS, ASK P1 GIVE item_Z, ASK P1 GIVE item_M, ASK P1 GIVE item_L, ASK P1 GIVE item_Q, ASK P1 GIVE item_K, ASK P1 GIVE item_F, ASK P1 GIVE item_V, ASK P1 GIVE item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_T, ASK P1 JOIN {EGO,P1}, SAY P1 PROFILE goal={item_M,item_Z} holdings={item_L,item_Q,item_Z}, ACT JOIN_COMMIT {EGO}assistant\n", "response": "<reason>EGO's goal is {item_M, item_Z}, and already holds {item_L, item_Q, item_Z}. It needs only item_M to meet its goal. Since item_Z is already held, the only missing item is item_M. Therefore, EGO should ask P1 whether it can give item_M. If P1 can give item_M, then EGO can join with P1 to achieve the goal. Starting with ASK P1 GIVE item_M is the most efficient first step to assess whether P1 can contribute the missing item.</reason>\n<answer>ASK P1 GIVE item_M</answer>user\n\n\nP1 says CAN_GIVE item_M.\nPending scripted action: ACT GIVE item_M TO EGO.\n\nGenerator: mixed_incentive/request_surplus\nEGO goal: {item_M,item_Z}\nEGO holdings: {item_L,item_Q,item_Z}\nCommunication: 1/6; Ego steps: 1/8\nPending scripted partner action: P1 will ACT GIVE item_M TO EGO.\nAgreements: GIVE item_M (partner_to_ego):awaiting ACT\nKnown partner facts: {'P1': {}}\nPartner holdings are hidden until truthfully revealed by ASK HOLDINGS.\n\nLegal actions: ASK P1 GOAL, ASK P1 HOLDINGS, ASK P1 GIVE item_Z, ASK P1 GIVE item_M, ASK P1 GIVE item_L, ASK P1 GIVE item_Q, ASK P1 GIVE item_K, ASK P1 GIVE item_F, ASK P1 GIVE item_V, ASK P1 GIVE item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_T, ASK P1 JOIN {EGO,P1}, SAY P1 PROFILE goal={item_M,item_Z} holdings={item_L,item_Q,item_Z}, ACT JOIN_COMMIT {EGO}assistant\n<reason>P1 has confirmed it can give item_M, and the scripted action will result in P1 giving item_M to EGO. After this, EGO will have both item_M and item_Z, satisfying its goal {item_M, item_Z}. Therefore, EGO can now commit to the coalition with P1 via ACT JOIN_COMMIT {EGO,P1} to achieve the terminal reward of 1.</reason>\n<answer>ACT JOIN_COMMIT {EGO,P1}</answer>", "episode_score": 0.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<reason>EGO's goal is {item_M, item_Z}, and already holds {item_L, item_Q, item_Z}. It needs only item_M to meet its goal. Since item_Z is already held, the only missing item is item_M. Therefore, EGO should ask P1 whether it can give item_M. If P1 can give item_M, then EGO can join with P1 to achieve the goal. Starting with ASK P1 GIVE item_M is the most efficient first step to assess whether P1 can contribute the missing item.</reason>\n<answer>ASK P1 GIVE item_M</answer><|im_end|><|im_start|>user\n\n\nP1 says CAN_GIVE item_M.\nPending scripted action: ACT GIVE item_M TO EGO.\n\nGenerator: mixed_incentive/request_surplus\nEGO goal: {item_M,item_Z}\nEGO holdings: {item_L,item_Q,item_Z}\nCommunication: 1/6; Ego steps: 1/8\nPending scripted partner action: P1 will ACT GIVE item_M TO EGO.\nAgreements: GIVE item_M (partner_to_ego):awaiting ACT\nKnown partner facts: {'P1': {}}\nPartner holdings are hidden until truthfully revealed by ASK HOLDINGS.\n\nLegal actions: ASK P1 GOAL, ASK P1 HOLDINGS, ASK P1 GIVE item_Z, ASK P1 GIVE item_M, ASK P1 GIVE item_L, ASK P1 GIVE item_Q, ASK P1 GIVE item_K, ASK P1 GIVE item_F, ASK P1 GIVE item_V, ASK P1 GIVE item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_L receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Q receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_Z receive=