ner then performs its scripted ACT GIVE to EGO. ASK EXCHANGE only forms an agreement. Execute an accepted exchange with ACT GIVE for your item; the partner then gives the agreed receive item; do not use a separate ACT form for exchange. If a partner asks EGO to GIVE an item, the next decision must be SAY CAN_GIVE or SAY CANNOT_GIVE. CAN_GIVE does not transfer the item; follow it with ACT GIVE. A JOIN agreement is not a commit: every listed partner must agree, then output the exact same ACT JOIN_COMMIT coalition. The episode ends at JOIN_COMMIT or after eight Ego steps.\n\nReason briefly inside <reason>...</reason>, then emit exactly one listed action inside <answer>...</answer>.\n\nGenerator: resource_conflict/cannot_help\nEGO goal: {item_M,item_Q}\nEGO holdings: {item_M,item_V}\nCommunication: 0/6; Ego steps: 0/8\nKnown partner facts: {'P1': {}, 'P2': {}}\nPartner holdings are hidden until truthfully revealed by ASK HOLDINGS.\n\nLegal actions: ASK P1 GOAL, ASK P1 HOLDINGS, ASK P1 GIVE item_M, ASK P1 GIVE item_Q, ASK P1 GIVE item_V, ASK P1 GIVE item_Z, ASK P1 GIVE item_L, ASK P1 GIVE item_F, ASK P1 GIVE item_K, ASK P1 GIVE item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_M receive=item_T, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_M, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_Q, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_V, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_Z, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_L, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_F, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_K, ASK P1 EXCHANGE give=item_V receive=item_T, ASK P1 JOIN {EGO,P1}, ASK P1 JOIN {EGO,P1,P2}, SAY P1 PROFILE goal={item_M,item_Q} holdings={item_M,item_V}, ASK P2 GOAL, ASK P2 HOLDINGS, ASK P2 G